{
  "openapi": "3.0.3",
  "info": {
    "description": "###  Introduction\n\nThis guide is meant to be used by developers working for restaurants.\n\nThis API allows your customers (the restaurants) to get availabilities and manage reservations.\n\n### How to authenticate calls from the Restaurant to TheFork\n\nWe use <a href='https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/authentication-and-authorization-flow/client-credentials-flow'>**Auth0's** Client Credentials Flow</a> to grant access to our API.\n\nIn order to access the `B2B API`, we will send you through a safe channel an **client_id** and **client_secret**.\n\nYou can use them to generate a **token**, by doing the following call:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST \\\n https://auth.thefork.io/oauth/token \\\n    -d 'audience=https://api.thefork.io&grant_type=client_credentials&client_id=YOUR_CLIENT_ID&client_secret=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET'\n```\n\nThe response will contain an `access_token`, needed for the calls to the API.\n\nThis token **expires** in 30 minutes. When it does, repeat this process to get a new token.\n\nIn order to use the API, please insert your `access_token` into the **headers** of your request as follows:\n\n```\ncurl https://api.thefork.io/manager/{version}/{path} \\\n    -H 'Authorization: Bearer <access_token>'\n```\n\n\n### Versioning\n\nWe use one version for the whole API, not one version per endpoint. Any breaking change to the contract of one or more endpoints will introduce a new version for our API.\n\nWe will stop supporting the previous version after 6 months.\n\n### Rate limiting\n\nCurrently rate limiting is enforced on default level, as specified in your contract. Please contact us to discuss your requirements if this needs revision.\n\n### <a name=\"errors\"></a>Errors\n\nTheFork uses conventional HTTP response codes for the success and failure of API requests.\n\nCertain **errors** can happen on **every** **endpoint** and should be caught globally, such as:\n\n- **429 (Rate limit)**\n- **401 (Invalid Bearer token)**\n\n```\n\n{\n\"statusCode\": 401,\n\"error\": \"Unauthorized\"\n}\n\n```\n\n- **500 - Internal server error**\n  General error, something went wrong\n\n```\n\n{\n\"statusCode\": 500,\n\"error\": \"Internal server error\"\n}\n\n```\n",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "title": "TFM B2B API v1"
  },
